; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Angles Explained
; CATEGORY: Geometry & Trigonometry
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     angles, degrees, arc, labels
; SUMMARY:  Draws an acute, a right, an obtuse and a reflex angle side by side, each with its arc and its size in degrees.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Four little pictures appear in a row. Each one has two arms that
;   meet at a corner, a colored arc that shows how far the second arm
;   turned, and a label with the angle and its name.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. To see another angle, type for example
;     angle.picture 0 0 135
;   in the command center after a CLEARSCREEN.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * an angle is an amount of turning, measured in degrees
;   * RIGHT turns the turtle clockwise, so a turn is an angle
;   * ARC draws part of a circle around the turtle
;   * IFELSE chains that pick a name from a number
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change the four numbers at the bottom to 30, 90, 150 and 300.
;   * Draw a straight angle (180) and see why it is called straight.
;   * Make the arms longer by changing :arm in angle.picture.
; ============================================================

; Pick the name that goes with an angle size.
to angle.name :deg
  if :deg < 90 [output "acute]
  if :deg = 90 [output "right]
  if :deg < 180 [output "obtuse]
  if :deg = 180 [output "straight]
  output "reflex
end

; Draw one angle with its corner at x y.
; The first arm points to the right (heading 90). The second arm is the
; first arm turned counterclockwise by :deg, just like a protractor.
to angle.picture :x :y :deg
  localmake "arm 70
  ; the turning arc: ARC sweeps clockwise from the heading, so we
  ; start it from the second arm and sweep back down to the first
  penup setxy :x :y pendown
  setpensize 6 setpencolor "orange
  setheading 90 - :deg
  arc :deg 25
  ; the two arms in dark blue
  setpensize 3 setpencolor [20 40 120]
  setheading 90 forward :arm back :arm
  setheading 90 - :deg forward :arm back :arm
  ; a small black dot marks the corner, which is called the vertex
  setpensize 8 setpencolor "black
  dot list :x :y
  ; the label sits underneath
  setpensize 1
  penup setxy :x - 40 :y - 100
  setheading 0
  label (sentence :deg "degrees)
  penup setxy :x - 40 :y - 120
  label angle.name :deg
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 248 240]
setlabelheight 16
angle.picture -300 0 40
angle.picture -110 0 90
angle.picture 80 0 130
angle.picture 270 0 250
penup setxy -230 180 setpencolor "black
setlabelheight 24
label [An angle is how far you turn]
